.TH io_receivefd 3
.SH NAME
io_receivefd \- receive a file descriptor over a Unix Domain socket
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <io.h>

int64 \fBio_receivefd\fP(fd_type \fIsock\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
io_receivefd receives a file descriptor that the peer sent with
io_passfd(3) over the Unix Domain socket \fIsock\fR.  The descriptor is a
new one in this process, referring to the same open file as the peer's.

io_receivefd blocks until the peer has sent one, unless \fIsock\fR is
non-blocking.
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
io_receivefd returns the new descriptor, or -1 on error (setting errno
accordingly).  If a byte arrives without a descriptor, errno is EPROTO.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
io_passfd(3)
